{"step_index":961,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T05:33:56Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-04T23:33:56-06:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-04T23:33:57-06:00\nPartial read (lines 540-600 of 960). Showing bytes 0-46080 of 122755 in this line range, truncated at the 46080-byte limit. To read the rest of this line range, call this tool again with the same StartLine and EndLine and ByteOffset=46080.\n540: {\"step_index\":539,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T06:42:28Z\",\"input_tokens\":2927,\"cache_read_tokens\":216148,\"output_tokens\":2086,\"thinking\":\"The log indicates a potential upgrade sequence being triggered. The mention of \\\"active slot = 0\\\" and an \\\"integer compare\\\" suggests a check or validation during this process. This observation requires further investigation to determine if it is relevant to the current problem.\\n\\n\\nThe \\\"detect upgrade key\\\" message is directly tied to the `itest` command's behavior within the U-Boot environment. The `itest` command, due to an undefined environment variable (`upgrade_key_flag`), results in an unexpected argument count, leading to its usage message and a false return value, preventing the update sequence from triggering. Further investigation is needed to verify this hypothesis by comparing with an older U-Boot version where the update is successful.\\n\\n\\nThe older U-Boot version's behavior shows that holding RESET (GPIOAO_3 == 0) triggers the upgrade key detection, then the `itest` command with the undefined variable leads to the usage message. This condition, leading to the \\\"itest\\\" command failing, prevents the update sequence. This aligns with the boot logs observed where the kernel later restarts the system with the 'recovery' command.\\n\\n\\nThe newer U-Boot version (Sep 05 2023) does not enter the USB burn mode when RESET is held. Instead, it triggers a kernel reboot into recovery or fastbootd based on USB content. The \\\"StartDedicatedWorldCupHuntFromLockedFastboot\\\" failure on the user's test case is now understood: the instructions given were for the 2021 U-Boot, not the Sep 05 2023 version where the key check is broken. The critical question now is how a locked device with the newer U-Boot can be unlocked externally.\\n\\n\\nThe focus shifts to exploring potential vulnerabilities in `fastbootd` (PID_4EE7), Recovery, and Android to unlock the locked device. A test device entered `fastbootd` (PID_4EE7) after holding RESET while a USB drive with `factory_update_param.aml` was inserted. The immediate jump to U-Boot Fastboot (PID_0D02) after the detection of `fastbootd` prompts further investigation into the functionalities of `fastbootd` prior to the transition. The next step will involve examining the `fastbootd` and `recovery` binaries for available commands and attack vectors.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"$bytes = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes(\\\\\\\"c:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\andre\\\\\\\\OneDrive\\\\\\\\Desktop\\\\\\\\xview\\\\\\\\experimento\\\\\\\\11_VALIDACION_OTA_Y_FIRMWARE_ZTE\\\\\\\\system_bin_recovery\\\\\\\")\\\\n$ascii = [System.Text.Encoding]::ASCII.GetString($bytes)\\\\n[regex]::Matches($ascii, \\\\\\\"[ -~]{8,}\\\\\\\") | ForEach-Object { $_.Value } | Where-Object { $_ -match \\\\\\\"fastboot|udisk|factory_update|ubootenv|otg_device|lock|oem|flashing|last_QR|adb\\\\\\\" } | Select-Object -First 80\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Search system_bin_recovery for fastboot, udisk, ubootenv, and lock strings\\\"\"}}]}\n541: {\"step_index\":540,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-04T06:42:57Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-11-04T00:42:57-06:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-11-04T00:43:00-06:00\\nCommand exited with code 0.\\n\\nCommand output:\\n_ZNSt3__16chrono12steady_clock3nowEv\\r\\npthread_mutex_lock\\r\\n